// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the current size inclusive, then for every position from the index to the old size of the vector, the element at the next position is either null and the old element at that position was null, or it is equal to the old element at that position.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to the size of the vector, then for every valid index i from the insertion index to the old size of the vector, the element at position i+1 in the new state of the vector is either null and the old element at i was null, or it is equal to the old element at i.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the vector inclusive, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the vector, the element at the next position is either null if the original element was null, or it equals the original element at that position.
